<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 June, from 313 to 1966.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/licinius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/licinius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">313 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,713 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Licinius publishes the agreement known as the Edict of Milan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicomedia">Nicomedia</a>, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licinius">Licinius</a> issued the letter agreed with Constantine granting freedom of worship to Christians and all others. Confiscated church property was ordered returned.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-milan">Edict of Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1381">1381 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">645 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peasants' Revolt rebels enter London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wat Tyler's rebels crossed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Bridge and burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-gaunt">John of Gaunt</a>'s Savoy Palace. The next day they stormed the Tower and beheaded the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1525">1525 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">501 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Luther marries Katharina von Bora</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former monk married a former nun in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>. Their marriage became a model for the Protestant clerical household.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1625">1625 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">401 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Charles I marries Henrietta Maria of France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-england">Charles I of England</a> married the Catholic princess Henrietta Maria of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a>, months after his accession. She was queen until his execution in 1649 and was the mother of Charles II and James II and VII.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-england">Charles I of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1740">1740 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">286 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Oglethorpe begins the siege of St Augustine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-oglethorpe">James Oglethorpe</a>, founder of the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, began a British attack on St Augustine in Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-jenkins-ear">War of Jenkins' Ear</a>. The siege lasted until 20 July and ended in failure.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-oglethorpe">James Oglethorpe</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Marquis de Lafayette lands in South Carolina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The French officer Lafayette, coming to serve in the Continental Army, landed on North Island near Georgetown, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>, after a two-month voyage aboard the Victoire. He later commanded Continental Army troops at the decisive siege of Yorktown in 1781.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1886">1886 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ludwig II of Bavaria is found drowned</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after being declared insane and deposed, the builder of Neuschwanstein was found dead in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-starnberg">Lake Starnberg</a> with his psychiatrist. The circumstances have never been explained.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1966">1966 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court decides Miranda v. Arizona</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Court ruled that suspects must be told of their right to remain silent and to have a lawyer before police questioning. The 'Miranda warning' became standard practice.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 June <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-the-bald.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles the Bald</span><span class="tp">823–877</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/taejong-of-joseon"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Taejong of Joseon</span><span class="tp">1367–1422</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antoni-radziwill"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoni-radziwill.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Antoni Radziwiłł</span><span class="tp">1775–1833</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-antonio-paez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-antonio-paez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Antonio Páez</span><span class="tp">1790–1873</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-clerk-maxwell"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-clerk-maxwell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Clerk Maxwell</span><span class="tp">1831–1879</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/w-b-yeats"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/w-b-yeats.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">W. B. Yeats</span><span class="tp">1865–1939</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/boyko-borisov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/boyko-borisov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Boyko Borisov</span><span class="tp">b. 1959</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 13 June <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/veronica-gambara"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/veronica-gambara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Veronica Gambara</span><span class="tp">1485–1550</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-ii-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludwig-ii-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludwig II of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1845–1886</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
